- The fake stamps _stampAtRead messages at message-read time (review-run.test.ts:4809-4814). EARLY carries stampOffsetMs -1000 (:5705, :4902), so created is read time minus 1000 ms.
- EARLY passes created >= start (review-run.sh:1221) only when the message GET lands more than one second after the floored call entry. It then contributes tokens at :1252.
- Answer selection stays FINAL because calls[0] is unchanged. No filter is bypassed, and a fresh per-call session holds only current-call messages.
- Verdict: fixture timing artifact, not a real hole. The 45 expectation reflects r8 newest-only semantics and is stale under r9. It does not corrupt night-3 token data. Route to backlog row 4.15.

